														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1503508">
									

<p>If its effects are caused by an electromagnetic signal of some kind, it is possible to build a containment vessel which would block those. Considering the fact that the signal would necessarily need to be complex to have this sort of effect, the bit-rate would need to be high (if this thing really is pulsing every 7ns), which means that it would <em>not</em> be a ELF signal. And while VLF electromagnetic signals are hard to block, non-ELF signals can be. Build a thick box of appropriate metal (what metal is appropriate and the thickness varies depending on the frequency; lead will stop gamma rays, while something a sheet of aluminum foil will stop visible light), put the item in there, and then either sink it under a few hundred or more feet of water (which does not transmit non-ELF signals well) or stick it down at the bottom of a mile deep mineshaft. Problem solved.</p>
<p>While the Foundation might be willing to prop up a backwater dictatorship if there was a good reason, when cheaper, less disruptive, and more effective containment procedures are possible, then I don't see them doing that. I'd expect that sort of behavior out of the Chaos Insurgency perhaps, but the Foundation has a difficult enough time containing things without unnecessarily meddling in world politics.</p>
<p>Downvoted for unnecessary containment procedures and unneeded interference in world politics.</p>

							</div>

								
