			<div class="content" id="post-content-1503531">
									

<p>It's an easter-egg alluded to by the dissent at the bottom, but the Soviets tried to destroy it in 1957. They failed, and evacuated the area shortly thereafter instead. The Foundation doesn't think it can do better, and &#8212; unlike the Soviets &#8212; it doesn't have a nuclear weapon on-hand to try.</p>
<p><a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kyshtym_disaster">http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kyshtym_disaster</a></p>
<p>And actually, the artifact doesn't 'want' much. It was originally a device designed to keep pesky <em>Homo erectus</em> from making trouble. It just happens to have been overengineered, and the descendants of <em>Homo erectus</em> which it was designed to effect are now worldwide. Totalitarian conditioning mitigates its effects not because of its design, but on the principle of inoculation: it's a less powerful version of what thing is attempting to do to all man-kind.</p>

