			<div class="content" id="post-content-1504415">
									

<p>If the signal contains a certain amount of information per second, that's a bit rate BR<sub>a</sub>. If a certain amount of information is transmitted per second, that's also a bit rate, BR<sub>b</sub>.</p>
<p>By all rights BR<sub>a</sub> should be &gt;=BR<sub>b</sub>. It's not<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-514494-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-514494-1')">1</a></sup>. That's anomalous, but not nonsensical; in fact it seems to be a property of several informational SCPs.</p>
