														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1811391">
									

<p>I tend to have similar uneasy feelings when any fantasy rubs against actual human totalitarianism&#8212; say various stories where the Holocaust was an exercise in black magic/human sacrifice. Where I draw the line is at the question: &quot;Does the element of fiction actually excuse or absolve the human actors of their moral responsibility?&quot; Basically, if the Nazis were trying to summon Azathoth, it doesn't cross the line because the fictional Nazis still have responsibility for their acts. OTOH if Azatoth was possessing the Nazis, it would cross the line because it's now all Azathoth's fault.</p>
<p>So, by my own rule of thumb, this passes because the situation in North Korea isn't caused by the SCP, the situation just offers a convenient method of containment.</p>
<p>Edit: Just noticed the year of the OP, sorry for the necropost.</p>

